# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Git LFS tracking.
#
# WHY: data/raw holds ten CellProfiler exports totalling ~766 MB. Two files
# EXCEED GitHub's 100 MB hard limit and cannot be pushed as normal git objects
# at all: KZ203 (190.8 MB) and KZ227 (122.3 MB). Four more are above the 50 MB
# warning threshold: KZ222 (68.6 MB), KZ195 (71.0 MB), KZ198 (91.5 MB) and
# KZ223 (94.1 MB). The remaining four are below it: KZ191 (49.9 MB), KZ226
# (32.3 MB), KZ214 (30.0 MB), KZ216 (14.8 MB). Tracking the whole data/raw tree
# keeps the rule simple and future-proof: a re-export that grows past the limit
# will not silently break the push.
#
# LFS NOTE: `git lfs install` must be run once per clone BEFORE `git clone`,
# otherwise the working tree receives 130-byte pointer files instead of CSVs
# and every pipeline stage fails at read time with a tokenizing error.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/raw/**/*.csv filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Per-figure source tables: one is ~9.7 MB. Below GitHub's warning
# threshold, but tracked in LFS so the repo stays clone-fast for readers who
# only want the code.
data/reference/published_tables/*.csv filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Derived data and figures are regenerated by the pipeline and are NOT tracked
# (see .gitignore). Published figure PNGs kept for comparison live in
# docs/published_figures/ and are small enough for normal git.
*.png -text
